 @qeqeqeq2305  Yeap, the same thing happened to me last month. I was at this bar when this bunch of 'influencers' and Youtubers were trying to be funny. They pretend to mess up my order, served me beer with 60% of it being head/foam, .etc.  I didn't touch the drink and I just walked off and left the place without paying.

As I left, one of the influencer ran up to me and asked me if I will give them permission to be in their video and asked for my consent.  I said "f**king hell no. I will sue all of you if you do."  and he just gave a shocked face standing there looking at me as I walked away.

F**king clowns. Just because they are making content for their entertainment purposes doesn't mean they can waste our entire day/time. And just like that my Saturday was ruined by these clowns.

 @kymeana  I guess the issue with rude at the end of the day is that it's a personal thing. The 6 million people watching this CONAN video see her to be abrasive, rude, and ungrateful. We forget that she just wanted some food. She didn't want a funny comedic segment. She has a right to that and she acted on it by denying Conan. 

Does that make her any less rude? No, not at all. 

Regardless, we don't know that she's a bad person and it annoys me to see people saying they "hate" her when it could've been any one of us on a bad day. Maybe shes a just a bit bitchy. Thats her right.

 @AlvinGuoSubscribe  The Chinese place where I moved to is uhhh such a hit or miss. I prefer lean meat, and randomly get chewy bits of chicken.

 I'm a picky eater especially with meat! I would get in trouble at a Sicilian restaurant when I was a prep cook for wasting suspicious meat. Edit I meant so much! Yet my chicken was the best!

 I would argue with the owners like I am cutting out the nasty bits!!!
